-- ============================================================================
-- Seed: medications catalogue
-- ============================================================================
-- Source: WHO Model List of Essential Medicines, 24th list (2025).
--   https://www.who.int/publications/i/item/B09474
--   Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 IGO
--
-- 755 rows / 529 distinct medicines, one row per (name, dosage form),
-- extracted from the published list. `strengths` holds the formulation
-- strengths exactly as the WHO list prints them ('25 mg', '5 mg/mL in
-- 1 mL ampoule', '0.25 mg to 6.0 mg'), so selecting a medication can
-- offer its real strengths rather than making the doctor retype them.
--
-- Rows with a null `form` and no strengths are medicines the WHO list
-- names only as a therapeutic alternative to another entry (sertraline,
-- escitalopram, aripiprazole, lorazepam and similar). They are included
-- because they are commonly prescribed and should be findable; they
-- simply carry no formulation data of their own, so the UI will not
-- prefill a dosage for them.
--
-- This is a general medical catalogue, not a psychiatric one â€” the whole
-- WHO list is here, from anaesthetics to antiretrovirals.
--
-- Adapt freely: the WHO list is a model for national lists, not a
-- formulary. Delete what the clinic never prescribes and insert local
-- products as needed; free-text medication entry remains available in the
-- consultation form regardless.
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT targets medications_name_form_key.
-- ============================================================================

on conflict (name, coalesce(form, '')) do nothing;
